{"name":"Hickory Cliff","hex":"#7c6e6d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hickory","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various deciduous hardwood trees of the genera Carya and Annamocarya, one species of which, Carya illinoinensis, is the source of pecan nuts.","The wood of these trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hickory"},{"term":"cliff","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A vertical (or nearly vertical) rock face.","A point beyond which something abruptly fails or decreases in value, performance, etc."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Obsolete form of clef."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cliff"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hickory","blocks":[{"text":"Hickory is a common name for trees composing the genus Carya, which includes 19 species accepted by Plants of the World Online."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Carya_Morton_29-U-10.jpg/330px-Carya_Morton_29-U-10.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hickory","wikidata":"Q142788"},{"title":"Cliff","blocks":[{"text":"In geography and geology, a cliff or bluff or rock face is an area of rock which has a general angle defined by the vertical, or nearly vertical. Cliffs are formed by the processes of weathering and erosion, with the effect of gravity. Cliffs are common on coasts, in mountainous areas, escarpments and along rivers. Cliffs are usually composed of rock that is resistant to weathering and erosion. The sedimentary rocks that are most likely to form cliffs include sandstone, limestone, chalk, and dolomite. Igneous rocks such as granite and basalt also often form cliffs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/White_Cliffs_of_Dover_02.JPG/330px-White_Cliffs_of_Dover_02.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cliff","wikida